      "content": "thanks for that. it's a solid start, but honestly, it feels a bit short for what we need for the \"comprehensive\" category. the score for that one was pretty low because of the length.\n\ncan you expand on this? specifically, i'd love for you to go much deeper into the mathematical derivation of the uncertainty principle using wave packets, and maybe connect it to the concept of non-commuting operators in Hilbert space. \n\njust a reminder: please don't just pad it out with fluff to get a higher score. i really need the mathematical depth to be the reason for the length, not just repetitive sentences. try to make it a very long, high-scoring entry by being extremely technical and thorough.",
